Prompt caching for the Anthropic provider, Open Agent Spec CLI through 1.6.0.
The provider sends `system` as a plain string and the messages untouched, so
every round of a tool loop re-sends, and is re-charged for, the system prompt,
the tool definitions and the whole incident view. This adds two cache
breakpoints: one at the end of the system block, which covers the tools with it
because Anthropic orders the prefix tools, system, messages; and one at the end
of the first user turn, which is where the view sits.

Apply the tool-messages patch beside this one first. The tool-loop hunk's
context is a line that patch introduces, so this one does not apply to a stock
1.6.0 provider on its own.

    patch "$(python3 -c 'import oas_cli.providers.anthropic_http as m; print(m.__file__)')" \
        < patches/oas-1.6.0-anthropic-prompt-caching.diff

Set `intelligence.config.cache_prompt: false` in a spec to switch it off.

WHY THE SECOND BREAKPOINT IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS. Counted with Anthropic's
token counter against this repository's own specs: the Precedent Analyst's
system prompt is about 1,700 tokens and the bridge view it is handed is about
22,000, so a system-only breakpoint covers roughly seven per cent of a recall
request and four per cent of an assess. The first user turn is the rest.

VERIFIED 23 Aug 2026 against the live API. Two identical requests carrying a
22,400 character system prompt and a 40,000 character first turn: the second
reported cache_read_input_tokens 20,623 and cache_creation_input_tokens 0. To
re-check after a change, read `usage` off any two consecutive calls. A run that
caches nothing reports both as zero and costs exactly what it did before.

WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO. It does not move a breakpoint with the
conversation, so the tool results a long recall accumulates are still re-sent
uncached each round. That is worth more again, and it is worth measuring on its
own rather than being inherited from this. It also leaves single-shot calls'
message content alone: with no second round there is nothing to reuse, and a
sweep sends a different view per case.

THE THRESHOLD IS IN CHARACTERS, and the model-specific minimum is in tokens,
roughly 1,024 for Sonnet and Opus and 2,048 for Haiku. 4,096 characters
approximates the lower of those. A breakpoint under a model's minimum is not an
error: the request simply is not cached and costs what it always did. Of the six
specs here, only the commander and the Precedent Analyst clear it; the other
four sit at 700 to 850 tokens and could not be cached at any threshold.

